WEBVTT

00:00:20.933 --> 00:00:22.744
Previously on Supernatural.

00:00:25.543 --> 00:00:29.101
Take your brother outside as
fast as you can! Now Dean! Go!

00:00:30.446 --> 00:00:32.024
Mary! No!

00:00:33.784 --> 00:00:34.923
Dad's on a hunting trip.

00:00:36.048 --> 00:00:37.599
And he hasn't been home in a few days.

00:00:39.565 --> 00:00:40.964
I swore I was done hunting,

00:00:41.650 --> 00:00:43.146
I can't do this alone.

00:00:48.785 --> 00:00:50.089
We got work to do.

00:00:50.459 --> 00:00:51.722
This is dad's single

00:00:51.763 --> 00:00:53.039
Most valuable possession.

00:00:53.066 --> 00:00:55.371
Everything he knows about
every evil thing is in here.

00:00:55.413 --> 00:00:57.380
I think he wants us to
pick up where he left off.

00:00:57.421 --> 00:00:58.724
You know, saving people,

00:00:58.752 --> 00:00:59.836
Hunting things...

00:00:59.877 --> 00:01:00.755
Family business.

00:01:00.817 --> 00:01:01.283
No.

00:01:01.324 --> 00:01:02.696
I gotta find Jessica's killer.

00:01:02.737 --> 00:01:04.206
It's the only thing I can think about.

00:01:04.260 --> 00:01:06.108
Sam, you know we're
gonna find dad, right?

00:01:07.917 --> 00:01:09.310
Yeah, I know.

00:01:24.910 --> 00:01:25.740
Morning, daddy.

00:01:25.802 --> 00:01:27.179
Morning, sweetheart.

00:01:29.406 --> 00:01:31.674
All these workouts, Soph, I don't know.

00:01:31.799 --> 00:01:33.599
Guys don't like buff girls.

00:01:33.693 --> 00:01:36.561
Yeah, well, girls don't like
guys who still live at home.

00:01:43.465 --> 00:01:44.873
Be careful.

00:01:44.936 --> 00:01:46.031
I will.

00:03:22.337 --> 00:03:23.902
Can I get you anything else?

00:03:27.109 --> 00:03:28.674
Just the check, please.

00:03:28.772 --> 00:03:29.679
Okay.

00:03:34.452 --> 00:03:37.707
You know, Sam, we are allowed
to have fun once in a while.

00:03:40.538 --> 00:03:41.634
That's fun.

00:03:45.972 --> 00:03:47.990
Here, take a look at
this. I think I got one.

00:03:48.350 --> 00:03:49.930
Lake Manitoc, Wisconsin.

00:03:50.102 --> 00:03:51.729
Last week, Sophie Carlton,

00:03:51.828 --> 00:03:54.049
18, walks into the lake,

00:03:54.190 --> 00:03:55.317
Doesn't walk out.

00:03:55.364 --> 00:03:57.038
Authorities dragged the water.

00:03:57.116 --> 00:03:58.008
Nothing.

00:03:58.180 --> 00:04:01.048
Sophie Carlton is the third
Lake Manitoc drowning this year.

00:04:01.173 --> 00:04:02.941
None of the other
bodies were found, either

00:04:03.082 --> 00:04:04.224
They had a funeral two days ago.

00:04:04.286 --> 00:04:04.897
A funeral?

00:04:04.943 --> 00:04:06.977
Yes, they buried an empty coffin.

00:04:07.235 --> 00:04:10.114
For closure or whatever.

00:04:10.349 --> 00:04:11.428
Closure?

00:04:12.570 --> 00:04:13.508
What closure?

00:04:13.712 --> 00:04:15.480
People don't just disappear, Dean.

00:04:15.714 --> 00:04:17.670
Other people just stop looking for them.

00:04:19.458 --> 00:04:20.553
Something you want to say to me?

00:04:20.589 --> 00:04:23.327
The trail for dad. It's getting colder.

00:04:23.452 --> 00:04:24.031
Every day.

00:04:24.062 --> 00:04:26.080
What are we supposed
to do? I don't know.

00:04:26.299 --> 00:04:27.128
Something.

00:04:27.269 --> 00:04:28.411
Anything. No one.

00:04:28.620 --> 00:04:29.840
I'm sick of this attitude.

00:04:30.168 --> 00:04:31.749
You don't think I want to
find dad as much as you do?

00:04:31.780 --> 00:04:32.562
Yeah, I know you do it.

00:04:32.593 --> 00:04:35.269
I'm the one that's been with him every
single day for the past two years.

00:04:35.378 --> 00:04:37.569
While you've been off to
college going to pep rallies.

00:04:37.709 --> 00:04:38.898
We will find dad,

00:04:38.961 --> 00:04:41.167
But until then, we're
gonna kill everything bad,

00:04:41.307 --> 00:04:42.841
Between here and there.

00:04:43.654 --> 00:04:44.703
Okay?

00:04:51.361 --> 00:04:53.332
All right, Lake Manitoc.

00:04:54.036 --> 00:04:54.411
Hey.

00:04:54.521 --> 00:04:54.959
Huh?

00:04:55.006 --> 00:04:55.804
How far?

00:05:17.103 --> 00:05:17.963
Will Carlton?

00:05:18.339 --> 00:05:19.027
Yeah, that's right.

00:05:19.183 --> 00:05:20.247
I'm agent Ford.

00:05:20.428 --> 00:05:21.773
This is agent Hamill.

00:05:22.258 --> 00:05:24.042
We're with the U.S. Wildlife service.

00:05:31.344 --> 00:05:33.221
She was about 100 yards out.

00:05:34.848 --> 00:05:35.943
That's where she got dragged down.

00:05:36.006 --> 00:05:37.351
And you're sure she didn't just drown?

00:05:37.383 --> 00:05:37.821
Yeah.

00:05:37.868 --> 00:05:39.573
She was a varsity swimmer.

00:05:39.667 --> 00:05:41.450
She practically grew up in that lake.

00:05:42.576 --> 00:05:44.751
She's as safe out there
as in her own bathtub.

00:05:45.330 --> 00:05:46.597
So no splashing,

00:05:46.691 --> 00:05:47.802
No signs of distress?

00:05:47.849 --> 00:05:49.006
No, that's what I'm telling you.

00:05:49.183 --> 00:05:51.326
Did you see any shadows in the water,

00:05:52.171 --> 00:05:53.016
Maybe,

00:05:53.219 --> 00:05:55.659
Some dark shape breach the surface?

00:05:55.706 --> 00:05:57.724
No, again, she was really far out there.

00:05:57.818 --> 00:05:59.570
You ever see any strange
tracks by the shoreline?

00:05:59.601 --> 00:06:00.509
No, never.

00:06:00.618 --> 00:06:01.432
Why?

00:06:01.557 --> 00:06:02.903
What do you think's out there?

00:06:03.357 --> 00:06:05.641
We'll let you know as soon as we do.

00:06:07.878 --> 00:06:09.380
What about your father?

00:06:09.615 --> 00:06:11.070
Can we talk to him?

00:06:13.140 --> 00:06:13.782
Look.

00:06:13.891 --> 00:06:15.377
If you don't mind, I mean,

00:06:15.581 --> 00:06:18.100
He didn't see anything, and
he's kind of been through a lot.

00:06:18.991 --> 00:06:20.243
We understand.

00:06:26.598 --> 00:06:27.542
Now, I'm sorry, but,

00:06:27.568 --> 00:06:31.767
Why does the wildlife service
care about an accidental drowning?

00:06:31.902 --> 00:06:33.247
You sure it's accidental?

00:06:33.503 --> 00:06:35.489
Will Carlton saw
something grab his sister.

00:06:36.053 --> 00:06:37.195
Like what?

00:06:37.633 --> 00:06:38.665
Here, sit, please.

00:06:38.712 --> 00:06:41.748
There are no indigenous
carnivores in that lake.

00:06:41.990 --> 00:06:44.642
There's nothing even big
enough to pull down a person,

00:06:44.728 --> 00:06:46.574
Unless it was the Loch Ness monster.

00:06:47.427 --> 00:06:48.882
Yeah, right.

00:06:49.007 --> 00:06:53.075
Will Carlton was traumatized, and
sometimes the mind plays tricks.

00:06:53.502 --> 00:06:54.362
Still,

00:06:54.894 --> 00:06:58.461
We dragged that entire lake.
We even ran a sonar sweep,

00:06:58.889 --> 00:07:01.282
Just to be sure, and there
was nothing down there.

00:07:01.361 --> 00:07:03.410
That's weird, though.

00:07:03.817 --> 00:07:05.444
That's the third missing body this year.

00:07:05.527 --> 00:07:06.622
I know.

00:07:07.279 --> 00:07:09.063
These are people from my town.

00:07:09.251 --> 00:07:10.721
These are people I care about.

00:07:10.815 --> 00:07:11.644
I know.

00:07:13.026 --> 00:07:14.074
Anyway . . .

00:07:15.780 --> 00:07:17.031
All this.

00:07:18.361 --> 00:07:20.239
It won't be a problem much longer.

00:07:20.817 --> 00:07:21.866
What do you mean?

00:07:22.654 --> 00:07:24.188
Well, the dam, of course.

00:07:25.502 --> 00:07:26.691
Of course.

00:07:26.957 --> 00:07:27.864
The dam.

00:07:28.177 --> 00:07:29.210
It's, uh...

00:07:30.649 --> 00:07:31.494
It sprung a leak.

00:07:31.572 --> 00:07:32.699
It's falling apart,

00:07:33.309 --> 00:07:36.067
And the feds won't give
us the grant to repair it,

00:07:36.130 --> 00:07:37.820
So they've opened the spillway.

00:07:38.445 --> 00:07:40.229
In another six months,

00:07:40.839 --> 00:07:42.263
There won't be much of a lake.

00:07:42.513 --> 00:07:44.082
There won't be much of a town, either,

00:07:44.223 --> 00:07:45.287
But as federal wildlife,

00:07:45.412 --> 00:07:46.805
You already knew that.

00:07:47.509 --> 00:07:48.338
Exactly.

00:07:48.995 --> 00:07:50.935
Sorry, am I interrupting?

00:07:51.472 --> 00:07:52.692
I think come back later.

00:07:52.833 --> 00:07:54.835
Gentlemen, this is my daughter.

00:07:55.258 --> 00:07:56.447
It's a pleasure to meet you.

00:07:56.791 --> 00:07:57.714
I'm Dean.

00:07:58.090 --> 00:07:59.482
Andrea Bar. Hi.

00:07:59.686 --> 00:08:00.108
Hi.

00:08:00.332 --> 00:08:01.849
They're from the wildlife service,

00:08:02.459 --> 00:08:03.711
About the lake.

00:08:07.878 --> 00:08:09.208
Oh, hey, there.

00:08:09.494 --> 00:08:10.448
What's your name?

00:08:16.769 --> 00:08:18.099
His name is Lucas.

00:08:20.974 --> 00:08:21.850
Is he okay?

00:08:21.928 --> 00:08:23.555
My grandson's been through a lot.

00:08:24.478 --> 00:08:25.793
We all have.

00:08:26.669 --> 00:08:27.482
Well,

00:08:28.254 --> 00:08:29.818
If there's anything
else I can do for you,

00:08:29.835 --> 00:08:30.899
Please, let me know.

00:08:31.023 --> 00:08:31.774
Thanks.

00:08:32.655 --> 00:08:34.360
You know, now that you mentioned it,

00:08:34.454 --> 00:08:37.693
Could you point us in the direction
of a reasonably priced motel?

00:08:37.885 --> 00:08:40.592
Lake front motel, go around
the corner, it's two blocks up.

00:08:40.655 --> 00:08:41.374
Two.

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:43.001
Would you mind showing us?

00:08:44.394 --> 00:08:46.068
You want me to walk you two blocks?

00:08:46.146 --> 00:08:47.429
Not if it's any trouble.

00:08:48.038 --> 00:08:49.900
I'm headed that way anyway.

00:08:51.042 --> 00:08:53.092
I'll be back to pick up lucas at 3:00.

00:08:53.170 --> 00:08:54.922
We'll go to the park, okay, sweetie?

00:08:58.870 --> 00:08:59.981
Thanks again.

00:09:01.045 --> 00:09:02.265
So, cute kid.

00:09:02.625 --> 00:09:03.204
Thanks.

00:09:05.353 --> 00:09:06.824
Kids are the best, huh?

00:09:10.630 --> 00:09:11.960
There it is.

00:09:12.570 --> 00:09:14.072
Like I said, two blocks.

00:09:14.150 --> 00:09:14.917
Thanks.

00:09:15.730 --> 00:09:18.171
Must be hard with your
sense of direction,

00:09:18.547 --> 00:09:21.441
Never being able to find your
way to a decent pickup line.

00:09:22.979 --> 00:09:24.215
Enjoy your stay.

00:09:26.077 --> 00:09:27.204
"Kids are the best"?

00:09:27.803 --> 00:09:29.649
You don't even like kids. I love kids.

00:09:29.712 --> 00:09:31.949
Name three children that you even know.

00:09:38.676 --> 00:09:39.740
I'm thinking.

00:09:40.147 --> 00:09:42.650
So there's the three
drowning victims this year.

00:09:42.681 --> 00:09:43.620
And before that?

00:09:43.761 --> 00:09:46.530
Yeah, six more,

00:09:46.561 --> 00:09:48.141
Spread outover the past 35 years.

00:09:48.282 --> 00:09:50.081
Those bodies were
never recovered, either.

00:09:50.691 --> 00:09:52.178
If there is something out there,

00:09:52.328 --> 00:09:53.283
It's picking up its pace.

00:09:53.345 --> 00:09:54.863
So we got a lake monster on a binge?

00:09:54.910 --> 00:09:57.601
This whole lake monster
theory, it just bugs me.

00:09:57.867 --> 00:09:58.712
Why?

00:09:59.249 --> 00:10:01.001
Loch Ness, lake Champlain

00:10:01.032 --> 00:10:03.598
There are literally hundreds
of eyewitness accounts,

00:10:03.645 --> 00:10:05.507
But here, almost nothing.

00:10:05.835 --> 00:10:07.115
Whatever it is out there,

00:10:07.416 --> 00:10:08.777
Noone's living to talk about it.

00:10:09.028 --> 00:10:10.295
Wait, Bar,

00:10:10.550 --> 00:10:12.428
Christopher Bar, where have
I heard that name before?

00:10:12.459 --> 00:10:15.072
Christopher Bar, the victim in may.

00:10:16.730 --> 00:10:18.639
Christopher Bar was Andrea's husband,

00:10:18.934 --> 00:10:20.373
Lucas' father.

00:10:20.831 --> 00:10:21.708
Apparently,

00:10:21.942 --> 00:10:23.773
He took Lucas out swimming.

00:10:23.820 --> 00:10:27.246
Lucas was on a floating wooden
platform when Chris drowned,

00:10:27.543 --> 00:10:28.685
Two hours,

00:10:29.124 --> 00:10:30.970
Before the kid got rescued.

00:10:34.677 --> 00:10:36.711
Maybe we have an eyewitness after all.

00:10:37.196 --> 00:10:39.011
No wonder that kid was so freaked out.

00:10:40.330 --> 00:10:42.958
Watching one of your parents die
isn't something you just get over.

00:10:45.133 --> 00:10:46.385
Can we join you?

00:10:50.377 --> 00:10:51.801
I'm here with my son.

00:10:55.196 --> 00:10:56.432
Mind if I say hi?

00:10:58.786 --> 00:11:02.212
Tell your friend this whole "jerry
maguire" thing's not gonna work on me.

00:11:03.026 --> 00:11:04.700
I don't think that's what this is about.

00:11:07.991 --> 00:11:09.133
How's it going?

00:11:16.730 --> 00:11:18.826
Oh, I used to love these things.

00:11:25.495 --> 00:11:27.451
So crayons is more your thing?

00:11:27.983 --> 00:11:29.970
That's cool. Chicks dig artists.

00:11:32.425 --> 00:11:33.786
Hey, these are pretty good.

00:11:35.366 --> 00:11:37.431
You mind if I sit and
draw with you for a while?

00:11:37.874 --> 00:11:39.454
I'm not so bad myself.

00:11:48.964 --> 00:11:50.826
You know, I'm thinking you can hear me.

00:11:51.373 --> 00:11:52.797
You just don't want to talk.

00:11:53.345 --> 00:11:55.535
I don't know exactly
what happened to your dad,

00:11:56.637 --> 00:11:58.501
But I know it was something real bad.

00:12:02.005 --> 00:12:03.585
I think I know how you feel.

00:12:06.041 --> 00:12:08.325
When I was your age, I saw something.

00:12:15.208 --> 00:12:16.397
Anyway . . .

00:12:18.404 --> 00:12:21.221
Maybe you don't think
anyone will listen to you.

00:12:21.961 --> 00:12:22.947
Or, uh...

00:12:24.680 --> 00:12:25.963
Or believe you.

00:12:26.573 --> 00:12:28.341
I want you to know that I will.

00:12:29.749 --> 00:12:31.266
You don't even have to

00:12:31.360 --> 00:12:33.331
Say anything. You
could draw me a picture,

00:12:33.394 --> 00:12:34.740
About what you saw that day,

00:12:35.038 --> 00:12:36.274
With your dad,

00:12:37.572 --> 00:12:38.433
On the lake.

00:12:42.517 --> 00:12:43.425
Okay,

00:12:43.550 --> 00:12:44.535
No problem.

00:12:45.005 --> 00:12:46.022
This is for you.

00:12:47.148 --> 00:12:48.462
This is my family.

00:12:49.761 --> 00:12:50.997
That's my dad.

00:12:51.362 --> 00:12:52.206
That's...

00:12:53.912 --> 00:12:54.944
That's my mom.

00:12:55.715 --> 00:12:57.311
That's my geek brother,

00:12:58.203 --> 00:12:59.392
And that's me.

00:13:03.288 --> 00:13:04.977
All right, so I'm a sucky artist.

00:13:05.404 --> 00:13:06.765
I'll see you around, Lucas.

00:13:19.971 --> 00:13:22.912
Lucas hasn't said a
word, not even to me,

00:13:23.527 --> 00:13:24.623
Not since

00:13:25.577 --> 00:13:27.157
His dad's accident.

00:13:27.830 --> 00:13:28.972
Yeah, we heard.

00:13:29.254 --> 00:13:30.177
Sorry.

00:13:31.303 --> 00:13:33.102
What are the doctors saying?

00:13:33.220 --> 00:13:35.879
That it's a kind of
post-Traumatic stress.

00:13:35.973 --> 00:13:37.194
That can't be easy

00:13:37.350 --> 00:13:38.054
For either of you.

00:13:38.117 --> 00:13:39.619
We moved in with my dad.

00:13:40.589 --> 00:13:42.247
He helps out a lot.

00:13:44.242 --> 00:13:45.384
It's just...

00:13:46.964 --> 00:13:50.312
When I think about what Lucas
went through, what he saw...

00:13:52.659 --> 00:13:53.926
Kids are strong.

00:13:54.486 --> 00:13:56.504
You'd be surprised
what they can deal with.

00:13:57.302 --> 00:13:58.366
You know,

00:13:58.883 --> 00:14:00.494
He used to have such life.

00:14:00.776 --> 00:14:03.169
He was hard to keep up
with, to tell you the truth.

00:14:04.369 --> 00:14:05.761
Now he just sits there,

00:14:05.871 --> 00:14:08.483
Drawing those pictures,
playing with those army men.

00:14:08.880 --> 00:14:10.022
I just wish.

00:14:10.710 --> 00:14:11.805
Hey, sweetie.

00:14:17.318 --> 00:14:18.100
Thanks.

00:14:19.132 --> 00:14:20.259
Thanks, Lucas.

00:14:38.375 --> 00:14:39.627
Hey, dad.

00:14:41.019 --> 00:14:42.834
You should probably eat something.

00:14:44.982 --> 00:14:46.547
I'm gonna make some dinner, okay?

00:16:41.125 --> 00:16:42.189
So,

00:16:42.299 --> 00:16:44.317
I think it's safe to say
we can rule out Nessie.

00:16:44.520 --> 00:16:45.146
What do you mean?

00:16:45.229 --> 00:16:48.358
I just drove past the Carlton
house. There was an ambulance there.

00:16:48.561 --> 00:16:49.907
Will Carlton is dead.

00:16:50.141 --> 00:16:50.720
He drowned?

00:16:50.767 --> 00:16:52.379
Yep, in the sink.

00:16:53.098 --> 00:16:54.240
What the hell?

00:16:54.620 --> 00:16:56.858
So this isn't a creature. We're
dealing with something else.

00:16:56.905 --> 00:16:57.687
Yeah, but what?

00:16:57.734 --> 00:16:58.344
I don't know.

00:16:58.469 --> 00:16:59.611
A water wraith maybe?

00:16:59.846 --> 00:17:00.925
Some kind of demon?

00:17:01.137 --> 00:17:02.811
I mean, something that controls water

00:17:05.242 --> 00:17:06.791
water that comes from the Same source.

00:17:06.854 --> 00:17:07.667
The lake Yeah

00:17:07.699 --> 00:17:09.607
Which would explain why
it's upping the body count.

00:17:09.983 --> 00:17:12.877
The lake is draining. It'll be dry in
a few months. Whatever this thing is,

00:17:12.949 --> 00:17:14.388
Whatever it wants,

00:17:14.717 --> 00:17:15.577
It's running out of time.

00:17:15.609 --> 00:17:17.158
And if it can get through the pipes,

00:17:17.596 --> 00:17:18.602
It can get to anyone,

00:17:18.665 --> 00:17:19.603
Almost anywhere.

00:17:19.697 --> 00:17:21.700
This is gonna happen again soon.

00:17:21.981 --> 00:17:23.483
And we do know one other thing for sure.

00:17:23.515 --> 00:17:25.815
We know this has got something
to do with Bill Carlton.

00:17:25.877 --> 00:17:26.901
It took both his kids.

00:17:26.948 --> 00:17:28.199
And I've been asking around.

00:17:28.324 --> 00:17:29.560
Lucas' dad, Chris

00:17:30.045 --> 00:17:31.328
Bill Carlton's godson.

00:17:32.001 --> 00:17:33.753
Let's go pay Mr. Carlton a visit.

00:17:36.265 --> 00:17:37.532
Mr. Carlton?

00:17:40.254 --> 00:17:42.272
We'd like to ask you a few questions,

00:17:42.351 --> 00:17:43.039
If you don't mind.

00:17:43.102 --> 00:17:45.495
We're from the department I
don't care who you're with.

00:17:46.110 --> 00:17:48.614
I've answered enough questions today.

00:17:50.694 --> 00:17:53.432
Your son said he saw
something in that lake.

00:17:54.402 --> 00:17:55.560
What about you?

00:17:56.098 --> 00:17:57.663
You ever see anything out there?

00:17:59.149 --> 00:18:00.119
Mr. Carlton,

00:18:00.150 --> 00:18:02.106
Sophie's drowning and Will's death.

00:18:02.403 --> 00:18:03.874
We think there might be a connection,

00:18:03.968 --> 00:18:06.862
To you or your family.
My children are gone.

00:18:10.447 --> 00:18:11.214
It's...

00:18:14.358 --> 00:18:16.032
It's worse than dying.

00:18:23.285 --> 00:18:24.318
Go away...

00:18:25.976 --> 00:18:26.852
Please.

00:18:29.845 --> 00:18:31.081
What do you think?

00:18:32.051 --> 00:18:34.053
I think the poor guy's
been through hell.

00:18:34.836 --> 00:18:36.650
I also think he's not
telling us something.

00:18:36.682 --> 00:18:37.699
So now what?

00:18:40.499 --> 00:18:41.406
What is it?

00:18:45.114 --> 00:18:47.727
Maybe Bill's not the only
one who knows something.

00:18:58.454 --> 00:19:00.237
I'm sorry, but I don't
think it's a good idea.

00:19:00.337 --> 00:19:01.432
I just need to talk to him,

00:19:01.495 --> 00:19:02.559
Just for a few minutes.

00:19:02.731 --> 00:19:04.342
He won't say anything.

00:19:04.827 --> 00:19:06.454
What good's it gonna do? Andrea,

00:19:06.658 --> 00:19:08.269
We think more people might get hurt.

00:19:09.807 --> 00:19:11.215
We think something's
happening out there.

00:19:11.324 --> 00:19:13.953
My husband, the others,
they just drowned.

00:19:14.375 --> 00:19:15.095
That's all.

00:19:15.142 --> 00:19:16.300
If that's what you really believe,

00:19:16.362 --> 00:19:17.129
Then we'll go,

00:19:17.415 --> 00:19:19.386
But if you think there's
even a possibility

00:19:19.699 --> 00:19:21.483
That something else
could be going on here,

00:19:23.079 --> 00:19:24.549
Please let me talk to your son.

00:19:39.968 --> 00:19:41.251
Hey, Lucas.

00:19:42.773 --> 00:19:43.900
You remember me?

00:19:53.156 --> 00:19:54.705
You know, I, uh...

00:19:56.473 --> 00:19:58.773
I wanted to thank you
for that last drawing

00:20:01.928 --> 00:20:03.586
but the thing is

00:20:04.071 --> 00:20:05.448
I need your help again.

00:20:18.418 --> 00:20:20.061
How did you know to draw this?

00:20:23.038 --> 00:20:25.150
Did you know something
bad was gonna happen?

00:20:27.247 --> 00:20:28.295
Maybe you could

00:20:28.717 --> 00:20:30.250
Nod yes or no

00:20:30.344 --> 00:20:31.173
For me.

00:20:33.645 --> 00:20:34.693
You're scared.

00:20:39.869 --> 00:20:40.730
It's okay.

00:20:41.559 --> 00:20:42.732
I understand.

00:20:43.249 --> 00:20:44.610
See, when I was your age,

00:20:44.688 --> 00:20:47.176
I saw something real
bad happen to my mom,

00:20:49.934 --> 00:20:51.326
And I was scared, too.

00:20:54.116 --> 00:20:55.524
I didn't feel like talking,

00:20:55.915 --> 00:20:57.057
Just like you,

00:20:58.246 --> 00:20:59.795
But, see, my mom,

00:21:02.204 --> 00:21:04.269
I know she wanted me to be brave.

00:21:07.591 --> 00:21:09.249
I think about that every day.

00:21:14.431 --> 00:21:16.418
And I do my best to be brave.

00:21:20.397 --> 00:21:22.003
And maybe your dad

00:21:24.111 --> 00:21:25.707
Wants you to be brave, too.

00:21:47.668 --> 00:21:48.826
Thanks, Lucas.

00:21:53.696 --> 00:21:56.136
Andrea said the kid never drew
like that till his dad died.

00:21:56.230 --> 00:21:59.547
There are cases going
through a traumatic experience

00:21:59.735 --> 00:22:04.386
Could make certain people more sensitive
to premonitions, psychic tendencies.

00:22:04.397 --> 00:22:06.767
What if Lucas is
tapping into it somehow?

00:22:07.059 --> 00:22:09.030
It's only a matter of time
before somebody else drowns,

00:22:09.044 --> 00:22:10.702
So if you got a better lead, please.

00:22:11.458 --> 00:22:12.460
All right.

00:22:12.699 --> 00:22:13.654
We got another house to find.

00:22:13.670 --> 00:22:17.096
There's about a thousand yellow
two-Stories in this county alone.

00:22:17.722 --> 00:22:18.927
See this church?

00:22:19.381 --> 00:22:21.415
I bet there's less than a
thousand of those around here.

00:22:22.218 --> 00:22:25.002
Oh, college boy thinks he's so smart.

00:22:32.363 --> 00:22:33.709
You know, um...

00:22:35.570 --> 00:22:36.947
What you said about mom.

00:22:39.951 --> 00:22:41.703
You never told me that before.

00:22:42.251 --> 00:22:43.503
It's no big deal.

00:22:47.669 --> 00:22:50.219
Oh, god, we're not gonna have
to hug or anything, are we?

00:23:16.620 --> 00:23:18.263
We're sorry to bother you, ma'am,

00:23:18.325 --> 00:23:20.735
But does a little boy
live here by chance?

00:23:20.876 --> 00:23:21.877
He might wear

00:23:22.002 --> 00:23:23.082
A blue ball cap,

00:23:23.348 --> 00:23:24.709
Has a red bicycle.

00:23:25.578 --> 00:23:26.626
No, sir.

00:23:28.081 --> 00:23:30.349
Not for a very long time.

00:23:31.898 --> 00:23:34.652
Peter's been gone 35 years now.

00:23:37.591 --> 00:23:39.297
The police never

00:23:40.454 --> 00:23:43.255
I never had any idea what happened.

00:23:46.464 --> 00:23:48.483
He just disappeared.

00:23:49.161 --> 00:23:50.522
Losing him,

00:23:52.697 --> 00:23:53.635
You know,

00:23:55.129 --> 00:23:55.708
It's...

00:23:57.841 --> 00:23:59.702
It's worse than dying.

00:24:04.729 --> 00:24:06.482
Did he disappear from here,

00:24:06.544 --> 00:24:07.530
I mean, from this house?

00:24:07.608 --> 00:24:08.813
He was supposed to

00:24:09.658 --> 00:24:10.784
Ride his bike

00:24:11.050 --> 00:24:12.208
Straight home

00:24:12.302 --> 00:24:13.412
After school,

00:24:13.835 --> 00:24:15.352
And he never showed up.

00:24:32.326 --> 00:24:34.250
"Peter Sweeney and Billy Carlton,

00:24:34.521 --> 00:24:35.976
1970."

00:24:41.723 --> 00:24:43.053
You've taken everything,

00:24:45.572 --> 00:24:46.824
Everyone.

00:24:49.785 --> 00:24:51.084
I've got nothing left.

00:24:54.541 --> 00:24:56.012
I didn't understand.

00:24:58.191 --> 00:24:59.490
I didn't believe.

00:25:02.353 --> 00:25:03.698
Now I think I do.

00:25:06.098 --> 00:25:08.147
I think I finally know what you want.

00:25:13.221 --> 00:25:15.427
Okay, this little boy,
Peter Sweeney, vanishes,

00:25:15.474 --> 00:25:17.820
And this is all connected
to Bill Carlton somehow.

00:25:17.852 --> 00:25:19.776
Bill sure as hell seems
to be hiding something.

00:25:19.839 --> 00:25:21.262
And Bill, the people he loves

00:25:21.408 --> 00:25:22.253
They're all getting punished.

00:25:22.457 --> 00:25:23.865
So that Bill did something to Peter.

00:25:24.084 --> 00:25:25.210
What if Bill killed him?

00:25:25.711 --> 00:25:27.056
Peter's spirit would be furious.

00:25:27.135 --> 00:25:28.574
It'd want revenge. It's possible.

00:25:33.988 --> 00:25:35.537
Mr. Carlton!

00:25:38.666 --> 00:25:40.089
Hey. Check it out.

00:25:47.989 --> 00:25:50.148
Mr. Carlton! You need to come back!

00:25:51.353 --> 00:25:53.559
Come out of the water !
Turn the boat around!

00:26:07.364 --> 00:26:08.881
Baby, what's wrong?

00:26:12.011 --> 00:26:13.575
Sam, Dean.

00:26:14.394 --> 00:26:16.287
I didn't expect to see you here.

00:26:17.273 --> 00:26:19.181
So now you're on a first-Name basis.

00:26:20.308 --> 00:26:21.450
What are you doing here?

00:26:21.502 --> 00:26:22.706
I brought you dinner.

00:26:23.051 --> 00:26:25.961
I'm sorry, sweetheart. I
don't really have the time.

00:26:30.081 --> 00:26:31.786
I heard about Bill Carlton.

00:26:32.083 --> 00:26:34.446
Is it true? Is something
going on with the lake?

00:26:36.417 --> 00:26:38.185
Right now, we don't
know what the truth is,

00:26:38.451 --> 00:26:40.939
But I think it might be better
if you and lucas went on home.

00:26:43.874 --> 00:26:45.595
Lucas, hey, what is it?

00:26:45.845 --> 00:26:47.238
Lucas. Lucas.

00:26:47.488 --> 00:26:49.882
Lucas, it's okay. It's okay. Hey,

00:26:49.960 --> 00:26:52.404
Lucas, it's okay. It's okay.

00:27:14.856 --> 00:27:17.985
Okay, just so I'm clear, you see . . .

00:27:18.219 --> 00:27:19.142
Something

00:27:19.627 --> 00:27:21.161
Attack Bill's boat,

00:27:21.630 --> 00:27:22.835
Sending Bill,

00:27:24.238 --> 00:27:26.647
Who is a very good swimmer, by the way,

00:27:26.913 --> 00:27:28.196
Into the drink,

00:27:29.025 --> 00:27:30.746
And you never see him again?

00:27:33.107 --> 00:27:34.640
Yeah, that about sums it up.

00:27:34.687 --> 00:27:36.189
And I'm supposed to believe this,

00:27:36.236 --> 00:27:38.958
Even though I've already
sonar-Swept that entire lake

00:27:39.381 --> 00:27:41.665
And what you're describing is impossible

00:27:42.353 --> 00:27:44.652
And you're not really wildlife service?

00:27:45.939 --> 00:27:46.768
That's right,

00:27:47.018 --> 00:27:47.722
I checked.

00:27:48.004 --> 00:27:49.631
The department's never heard of you two.

00:27:50.137 --> 00:27:50.841
See?

00:27:50.935 --> 00:27:52.843
Now, we can explain that. Enough,

00:27:53.594 --> 00:27:54.674
Please.

00:27:55.816 --> 00:27:58.194
The only reason you're
breathing free air

00:27:58.449 --> 00:28:02.298
Is one of Bill's neighbors saw him
steering out that boat just before you did.

00:28:03.033 --> 00:28:03.691
So

00:28:03.925 --> 00:28:05.505
We have a couple of options here.

00:28:05.803 --> 00:28:07.988
I can arrest you for
impersonating government officials

00:28:08.004 --> 00:28:11.608
And hold you as material witnesses
to Bill Carlton's disappearance,

00:28:11.857 --> 00:28:12.670
Or

00:28:12.983 --> 00:28:15.799
We can chalk this all up to a bad day,

00:28:16.070 --> 00:28:17.525
You get into your car,

00:28:17.665 --> 00:28:20.548
You put this town in
your rearview mirror,

00:28:20.561 --> 00:28:23.704
And you don't ever darken my doorstep

00:28:23.762 --> 00:28:24.476
Again!

00:28:27.182 --> 00:28:28.746
Door number two sounds good.

00:28:28.997 --> 00:28:30.499
That's the one I'd pick.

00:28:45.428 --> 00:28:46.429
Baby...

00:28:48.267 --> 00:28:49.800
What are you doing up?

00:28:52.617 --> 00:28:54.353
Come on, let's go to bed.

00:29:15.668 --> 00:29:16.669
Green.

00:29:16.810 --> 00:29:17.498
What?

00:29:17.623 --> 00:29:19.016
Light's green.

00:29:26.295 --> 00:29:28.126
Ah, the interstate's the other way.

00:29:28.157 --> 00:29:28.767
I know.

00:29:53.056 --> 00:29:55.481
But, Dean, this job, I think it's over.

00:29:55.528 --> 00:29:56.372
I'm not so sure.

00:29:56.419 --> 00:29:59.439
If bill murdered Peter Sweeney
and Peter's spirit got its revenge,

00:29:59.595 --> 00:30:01.692
Case closed. The spirit
should be at rest.

00:30:01.737 --> 00:30:04.053
All right, so what if we take
off and this thing isn't done?

00:30:04.350 --> 00:30:06.374
What if we missed something?
What if more people get hurt?

00:30:06.452 --> 00:30:08.032
But why would you think that?

00:30:09.846 --> 00:30:11.520
Because Lucas was really scared.

00:30:11.786 --> 00:30:13.273
That's what this is about?

00:30:14.243 --> 00:30:16.574
I just don't want to leave
town till I know the kid's okay.

00:30:17.043 --> 00:30:18.029
Who are you,

00:30:18.138 --> 00:30:19.969
And what have you done with my brother?

00:30:22.346 --> 00:30:23.551
Shut up.

00:31:53.888 --> 00:31:55.343
Are you sure about this?

00:31:55.671 --> 00:31:56.970
It's pretty late, man.

00:32:00.291 --> 00:32:01.762
Lucas? Lucas!

00:32:04.703 --> 00:32:05.626
Lucas!

00:32:44.697 --> 00:32:45.761
Can you tell me?

00:32:47.893 --> 00:32:48.754
No

00:32:56.798 --> 00:32:58.503
It doesn't make any sense.

00:33:02.602 --> 00:33:04.135
I'm going crazy.

00:33:05.152 --> 00:33:06.671
No, you're not.

00:33:08.095 --> 00:33:09.269
Tell me what happened.

00:33:09.879 --> 00:33:10.818
Everything.

00:33:15.008 --> 00:33:16.134
I heard...

00:33:19.107 --> 00:33:20.844
I thought I heard...

00:33:23.152 --> 00:33:24.967
There was this voice.

00:33:25.483 --> 00:33:26.453
What did it say?

00:33:26.500 --> 00:33:27.345
It said

00:33:28.305 --> 00:33:30.558
It said, "come play with me."

00:33:38.550 --> 00:33:40.052
What's happening?

00:33:59.342 --> 00:34:01.157
Do you recognize the
kids in these pictures?

00:34:01.282 --> 00:34:02.033
What?

00:34:03.942 --> 00:34:04.834
No, I huh...

00:34:04.912 --> 00:34:08.025
I mean, except that's
my dad right there.

00:34:08.233 --> 00:34:09.594
He must have been about

00:34:10.204 --> 00:34:11.831
12 in these pictures.

00:34:13.460 --> 00:34:14.821
Chris Bar's drowning

00:34:15.102 --> 00:34:17.465
The connection wasn't to Bill
Carlton. It must have been to sheriff.

00:34:17.527 --> 00:34:18.982
Bill and the sheriff,

00:34:19.342 --> 00:34:20.954
They were both involved with Peter.

00:34:21.225 --> 00:34:22.252
What about Chris?

00:34:22.867 --> 00:34:25.026
My dad, what are you talking about?

00:34:25.261 --> 00:34:26.153
Lucas?

00:34:26.873 --> 00:34:28.202
Lucas, what is it?

00:34:34.509 --> 00:34:36.684
Lucas, honey?

00:34:48.441 --> 00:34:50.881
You and Lucas get back to the
house and stay there, okay?

00:35:15.183 --> 00:35:16.435
Peter's bike.

00:35:17.233 --> 00:35:18.281
Who are you?

00:35:21.676 --> 00:35:23.162
Put the gun down, Jake.

00:35:23.866 --> 00:35:25.341
How did you know that was there?

00:35:25.388 --> 00:35:26.233
What happened?

00:35:26.437 --> 00:35:27.985
You and Bill killed Peter,

00:35:28.330 --> 00:35:30.176
Drowned him in the lake,
and then buried the bike?

00:35:31.130 --> 00:35:32.851
You can't bury the truth, Jake.

00:35:34.030 --> 00:35:35.657
Nothing stays buried.

00:35:39.224 --> 00:35:40.726
Go to your room, sweetie.

00:35:42.009 --> 00:35:42.854
Now.

00:35:42.901 --> 00:35:45.172
Lock the door and wait
for me. Don't come out.

00:35:45.546 --> 00:35:46.907
I don't know what the
hell you're talking about.

00:35:46.929 --> 00:35:49.348
You and Bill killed Peter
Sweeney 35 years ago.

00:35:49.442 --> 00:35:50.360
That's what the hell I'm talking about.

00:35:50.365 --> 00:35:50.975
Dad

00:35:51.256 --> 00:35:53.337
And now you got one
seriously pissed-Off spirit.

00:35:53.384 --> 00:35:54.636
It's gonna take Andrea,

00:35:54.745 --> 00:35:55.527
Lucas,

00:35:55.827 --> 00:35:56.812
Everyone you love.

00:35:57.313 --> 00:35:58.393
It's gonna drown them,

00:35:58.799 --> 00:36:00.661
And it's gonna drag their
bodies god knows where.

00:36:00.958 --> 00:36:03.227
So you can feel the Same
pain Peter's mom felt.

00:36:04.088 --> 00:36:05.386
And then after that,

00:36:06.276 --> 00:36:07.325
It's gonna take you,

00:36:07.638 --> 00:36:09.359
And it's not gonna stop until it does.

00:36:10.250 --> 00:36:11.314
How do you know that?

00:36:11.424 --> 00:36:13.880
Because that's exactly
what it did to Bill Carlton.

00:36:13.927 --> 00:36:15.072
Listen to yourselves,

00:36:15.323 --> 00:36:15.933
Both of you.

00:36:15.995 --> 00:36:17.122
You're insane.

00:36:17.169 --> 00:36:19.359
I don't really give a rat's
ass what you think of us,

00:36:20.367 --> 00:36:22.010
But if we're gonna
bring down this spirit,

00:36:22.229 --> 00:36:23.778
We need to find the remains,

00:36:24.044 --> 00:36:24.857
Salt them,

00:36:24.998 --> 00:36:26.125
And burn them into dust.

00:36:26.328 --> 00:36:27.840
Tell me you buried Peter somewhere.

00:36:27.862 --> 00:36:29.593
Tell me you didn't just
let him go in the lake.

00:36:34.960 --> 00:36:37.651
Come play with me.

00:36:41.520 --> 00:36:42.083
Dad,

00:36:42.146 --> 00:36:43.178
Is any of this true?

00:36:43.209 --> 00:36:44.461
No. Don't listen to them.

00:36:44.487 --> 00:36:45.791
They're liars, and they're dangerous.

00:36:45.947 --> 00:36:47.574
Something tried to drown me.

00:36:48.122 --> 00:36:49.405
Chris died on that lake.

00:36:49.436 --> 00:36:50.578
Dad, look at me.

00:36:53.894 --> 00:36:54.566
Tell me you

00:36:54.629 --> 00:36:56.162
You didn't kill anyone.

00:37:06.050 --> 00:37:07.161
Oh, my god.

00:37:11.213 --> 00:37:12.709
Billy and I were at the lake.

00:37:15.791 --> 00:37:18.420
Peter was the smallest
one. We always bullied him,

00:37:18.952 --> 00:37:20.062
But this time...

00:37:21.319 --> 00:37:22.414
It got rough.

00:37:27.343 --> 00:37:28.985
We were holding his
head under the water.

00:37:29.882 --> 00:37:31.134
We didn't mean to,

00:37:31.963 --> 00:37:33.653
But we held him under too long,

00:37:33.778 --> 00:37:34.983
And he drowned.

00:37:41.975 --> 00:37:43.289
We let the body go,

00:37:44.009 --> 00:37:45.073
And it sank.

00:37:52.146 --> 00:37:53.382
Oh, Andrea.

00:37:56.485 --> 00:37:57.659
We were kids.

00:37:58.159 --> 00:37:59.051
We were so scared.

00:37:59.082 --> 00:38:00.099
It was a mistake,

00:38:00.115 --> 00:38:00.970
But, Andrea,

00:38:01.262 --> 00:38:03.671
To say that I have anything
to do with these drownings,

00:38:03.702 --> 00:38:04.829
With Chris,

00:38:05.251 --> 00:38:06.894
Because of some ghost

00:38:07.176 --> 00:38:08.725
It's not rational.

00:38:09.746 --> 00:38:11.013
All right, listen to me,

00:38:11.514 --> 00:38:12.468
All of you.

00:38:13.141 --> 00:38:14.643
We need to get you away from this lake

00:38:14.737 --> 00:38:16.379
As far as we can right now.

00:38:20.304 --> 00:38:20.882
Lucas!

00:38:24.705 --> 00:38:26.754
Come play with me.

00:38:27.662 --> 00:38:28.444
Lucas!

00:38:28.636 --> 00:38:31.327
Lucas! Stay where you are!

00:38:50.315 --> 00:38:51.410
Oh, my god!

00:38:54.883 --> 00:38:56.072
Andrea, stay there.

00:38:56.213 --> 00:38:57.293
No, Lucas!

00:38:57.345 --> 00:38:58.643
We'll get him. Stay on the dock.

00:39:04.929 --> 00:39:05.904
Lucas?

00:39:08.622 --> 00:39:09.420
Sam?

00:39:11.313 --> 00:39:12.862
Lucas, where are you?

00:39:17.138 --> 00:39:17.764
Peter,

00:39:17.936 --> 00:39:18.906
If you can hear me,

00:39:20.068 --> 00:39:21.006
Please, Peter,

00:39:21.038 --> 00:39:21.789
I'm sorry.

00:39:23.275 --> 00:39:24.104
I'm so... Dad, no!

00:39:24.151 --> 00:39:25.215
I'm so sorry.

00:39:25.716 --> 00:39:26.279
Peter.

00:39:26.514 --> 00:39:27.202
Lucas

00:39:27.499 --> 00:39:29.658
He's j... he's just a little boy.

00:39:30.367 --> 00:39:32.448
Please, it's not his fault. It's mine.

00:39:32.589 --> 00:39:33.762
Please take me!

00:39:34.763 --> 00:39:35.311
Jake,

00:39:35.373 --> 00:39:35.733
No!

00:39:37.032 --> 00:39:38.487
Listen, let it be over!

00:39:40.748 --> 00:39:41.436
Dad

00:39:42.268 --> 00:39:43.099
Daddy!

00:39:45.632 --> 00:39:46.492
No

00:39:56.486 --> 00:39:57.346
No...

00:40:37.737 --> 00:40:38.473
Look,

00:40:39.302 --> 00:40:40.679
We're not gonna save everybody.

00:40:43.312 --> 00:40:43.969
I know.

00:40:44.751 --> 00:40:45.502
Sam,

00:40:45.878 --> 00:40:46.566
Dean.

00:40:46.707 --> 00:40:47.473
Hey.

00:40:49.194 --> 00:40:50.352
We're glad we caught you.

00:40:50.790 --> 00:40:51.682
We just, um,

00:40:52.875 --> 00:40:54.377
We made you lunch for the road.

00:40:55.159 --> 00:40:57.897
Lucas insisted on making
the sandwiches himself.

00:40:59.372 --> 00:41:00.421
Can I give it to them now?

00:41:02.345 --> 00:41:02.955
Of course.

00:41:04.174 --> 00:41:05.989
Come on, Lucas, let's
load this in the car.

00:41:12.611 --> 00:41:13.549
How you holding up?

00:41:15.990 --> 00:41:18.916
It's just gonna take a long time to
sort through everything, you know?

00:41:22.863 --> 00:41:24.459
Andrea, I'm sorry.

00:41:26.054 --> 00:41:27.259
You saved my son.

00:41:29.043 --> 00:41:30.779
I can't ask for more than that.

00:41:34.454 --> 00:41:35.315
Dad loved me.

00:41:36.441 --> 00:41:37.693
He loved Lucas.

00:41:38.679 --> 00:41:39.680
No matter what he did,

00:41:39.701 --> 00:41:40.822
I just have to...

00:41:42.579 --> 00:41:43.628
Hold on to that.

00:41:49.825 --> 00:41:50.643
All right,

00:41:50.806 --> 00:41:52.277
If you're gonna be talking now,

00:41:52.572 --> 00:41:55.580
This is a very important phrase, so
I want you to repeat it one more time.

00:41:55.776 --> 00:41:56.730
Zeppelin rules!

00:41:56.734 --> 00:41:58.140
That's right. Up high.

00:42:01.826 --> 00:42:03.786
Take care of your mom, okay?

00:42:11.731 --> 00:42:13.268
Thank you.

00:42:18.444 --> 00:42:19.719
Sam, move your ass.

00:42:20.112 --> 00:42:22.172
We're gonna run out of
daylight before we hit the road.



